      "extract": "The Gaussian density function, or simply Gaussian, is the two-variable function defined by KR (t,x) := 1 √ 4πt e−x2/4t for x ∈R and t ∈R+. (1) In common language the Gaussian is sometimes referred to as the bell-shaped curve. In prob- ability theory, (1) is the density function of a normal random variable. The universality of the Gaussian is evident from the classical central limit theorem, the theory of Brownian",
