      "extract": "Let X = (VX,EX) be a countable graph of bounded degree, where VX and EX denote the sets of vertices and edges, respectively. The Laplacian is an operator on L2(VX,C) defined by (∆Xf)(x) = X y∼x (f(x) −f(y)), (10) where the sum is taken over all vertices adjacent to x in X. A graph is called (q + 1)-regular or regular if every vertex has degree q + 1. The reason for the normalization of ‘q + 1’ comes form number",
