      "extract": "Let us continue with the setting of the last paragraph with p,q > 0 and p + q = 1. Then the heat kernel Kp,q(2t,x) with x ∈Z can be viewed as the probability distribution of the continuous- time random walk on Z which steps one unit to the left (resp. right) with probability p (resp. q = 1 −p.) Further, the time interval between steps has an exponential distribution with density 2e−2t, see [Fe66] or [Fe70, chapter",
