      "extract": "Bessel functions are ubiquitous in mathematical physics, perhaps first appearing as a solution to Bessel’s differential equations arising from the Laplace equation with cylindrical symmetry. A classic text on Bessel functions is Watson’s book [Wa44]. The fact that the I-Bessel func- tion is essentially a heat kernel makes many of the classical identities immediate from physical principles. Note that we continue to",
